WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:09.123
Once upon a time there was a young boy.

2
00:00:09.124 --> 00:00:11.467
He lived in a quiet village.

3
00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:13.892
All the village people had sheep.

4
00:00:13.893 --> 00:00:16.742
The boy's job was to watch the sheep.

5
00:00:16.743 --> 00:00:20.331
He had to protect them from wolves.

6
00:00:20.332 --> 00:00:24.752
Looking after the sheep was easy, but it was not fun.

7
00:00:24.753 --> 00:00:28.553
"I am so bored!" said the boy.

8
00:00:28.554 --> 00:00:33.369
"I want to have some adventure and excitement!"

9
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.461
Suddenly the boy had an idea.

10
00:00:36.462 --> 00:00:41.581
The boy took a deep breath, opened his mouth wide, and shouted,

11
00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:48.168
"Wolf! Wolf! Help! There's a wolf!"

12
00:00:48.169 --> 00:00:51.316
The whole village heard the boy's cry.

13
00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.405
They stopped what they were doing.

14
00:00:53.406 --> 00:00:56.796
Everyone was scared.

15
00:00:56.797 --> 00:00:59.648
The village people ran to the boy.

16
00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:00.925
"Where is it?

17
00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:04.114
Where is the wolf?" said the old man.

18
00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:07.502
"Are the sheep okay?" asked the woman.

19
00:01:07.503 --> 00:01:09.533
But there was no wolf.

20
00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.813
The boy was playing a trick.

21
00:01:11.814 --> 00:01:17.219
The village people were angry at the boy.

22
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.663
The next day, the boy was watching the sheep again.

23
00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:26.477
"It was so funny yesterday," he said.

24
00:01:26.478 --> 00:01:28.579
"I will have some more fun."

25
00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:33.757
The boy took a deep breath and shouted very loudly,

26
00:01:33.758 --> 00:01:41.139
"Wolf! There's a big scary wolf! Wolf!"

27
00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.104
The boy's cry was loud and clear.

28
00:01:44.105 --> 00:01:46.891
Everyone stopped what they were doing.

29
00:01:46.892 --> 00:01:50.676
Everyone was scared.

30
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.755
They ran to the boy.

31
00:01:52.756 --> 00:01:56.046
"Where is the wolf?" said the old man.

32
00:01:56.047 --> 00:01:58.784
But of course there was no wolf.

33
00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:07.015
The boy was playing a trick again.

34
00:02:07.016 --> 00:02:14.822
"Don't cry, 'Wolf!' when there is no wolf!" they shouted.

35
00:02:14.823 --> 00:02:19.475
Later that afternoon, the boy was getting ready to go home.

36
00:02:19.476 --> 00:02:22.595
Suddenly, he heard a strange sound.

37
00:02:22.596 --> 00:02:24.898
It was a real wolf!

38
00:02:24.899 --> 00:02:30.104
The boy took a deep breath and shouted as loud as he could,

39
00:02:30.105 --> 00:02:37.805
"Wolf! There's a big wolf! Help! Wolf!"

40
00:02:37.806 --> 00:02:41.348
Everyone heard the boy crying "wolf!"

41
00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:44.197
But they thought he was playing another trick.

42
00:02:44.198 --> 00:02:47.388
So nobody paid any attention to him.

43
00:02:47.389 --> 00:02:52.359
The wolf chased and ate the sheep.

44
00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.303
The next morning, the village people came to look for the boy.

45
00:02:57.304 --> 00:02:58.933
"Where are the sheep?

46
00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:02.349
What is going on?" asked the woman.

47
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.975
"There was a wolf!

48
00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:10.723
I called, 'Wolf!' but nobody came!" cried the boy.

49
00:03:10.724 --> 00:03:17.835
"When you called 'wolf!' the first two times, was there really a wolf?" asked the old man.

50
00:03:17.836 --> 00:03:21.123
"No," said the embarrassed boy.

51
00:03:21.124 --> 00:03:27.204
"Then why would we believe you when you really saw a wolf?" the old man explained.

52
00:03:27.205 --> 00:03:33.668
"Nobody believes a liar, even when he is telling the truth!"
